<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 06:23:40 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Russia and Ukraine trade blame for cyber attacks as fragile ceasefire ends</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-live-russia-and-ukraine-trade-blame-cyber-attacks-fragile-ceasefire-ends</link><description>
Russia and Ukraine on Monday traded accusations over cyberattacks, with Moscow reporting a hack of its emergency alerts app hours after Kyiv said its own air raid warning system had been compromised. The incidents came as a fragile ceasefire in Ukraine's Kherson region expired, raising fears of renewed fighting. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f8e22fe-d684-11f1-9056-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-30T222725Z-2094630474-RC2QDOAMPZAZ-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-KHERSON.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f8e22fe-d684-11f1-9056-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-30T222725Z-2094630474-RC2QDOAMPZAZ-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-KHERSON.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">372e232e-d684-11f1-bcc0-a99176443041</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 06:19:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f8e22fe-d684-11f1-9056-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-30T222725Z-2094630474-RC2QDOAMPZAZ-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-KHERSON.jpg">© Nina Liashonok, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Midterms 2026: Georgians on the front lines of the people’s war against data centres</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-midterms-2026-georgians-front-lines-people-war-against-data-centres</link><description>
Artificial intelligence emerged as a major issue on the 2026 US midterm campaign trail, with opposition to data centres drawing supporters across partisan divides united over ecological worries, increased utility bills and business interests outweighing citizen concerns. Georgia, the top US market for data centre construction, has been on the front line of the struggle. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7792b7ee-d491-11f1-b147-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/main-93.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7792b7ee-d491-11f1-b147-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/main-93.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9763282e-d491-11f1-9e9b-cb1f2e7eecaf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 06:11:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7792b7ee-d491-11f1-b147-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/main-93.jpg">© Mike Stewart, AP</source><dc:creator>Leela JACINTO</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia and Ukraine accuse each other of hacking emergency alert apps</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261102-ukraine-suspects-nationwide-air-raid-alert-app-has-been-hacked</link><description>
Russia and Ukraine accused each other of hacking their emergency alert applications as a local ceasefire in the war's eastern Kherson region expired on Sunday. The cyberattacks came as both sides warned of renewed fighting and Kyiv signalled it could halt strikes on Russian oil refineries in exchange for US Patriot missiles.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01e27286-d5fa-11f1-9fb6-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/6a3c233d865056dcf34ec2006538c9fc902893e3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01e27286-d5fa-11f1-9fb6-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/6a3c233d865056dcf34ec2006538c9fc902893e3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a0ced658-d65b-11f1-ae13-8b30643331f8</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 01:20:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01e27286-d5fa-11f1-9fb6-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/6a3c233d865056dcf34ec2006538c9fc902893e3.jpg">© Roman Pilipey, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Halloween weekend shootings across US leave at least six dead, dozens wounded</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-halloween-weekend-shootings-across-us-leave-at-least-six-dead-dozens-wounded</link><description>
A spate of shootings in nightlife districts and near university campuses across the United States over Halloween weekend left at least six people dead and dozens wounded, with Dallas recording the highest toll. Police were investigating multiple incidents in several states, while some suspects remained at large.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c665287a-bb41-11f1-9424-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-28T094246Z-237616975-RC28SNAUGKNH-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c665287a-bb41-11f1-9424-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-28T094246Z-237616975-RC28SNAUGKNH-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">32cb14f4-d657-11f1-904b-b798d30cad20</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 00:49:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c665287a-bb41-11f1-9424-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-28T094246Z-237616975-RC28SNAUGKNH-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg">© Toby Shepheard, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran warns renewed war with US could outlast previous conflict</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261102-iran-warns-renewed-war-with-us-could-outlast-previous-conflict</link><description>
Iran warned on Sunday that a renewed war with the United States could last longer than the previous conflict, as President Donald Trump suggested Washington still had targets to strike. Tehran threatened retaliation without geographical limits while diplomatic efforts continued to avert a fresh escalation ahead of Tuesday's US midterm elections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66662f02-d557-11f1-8301-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-PORTADA-IRAN-MOJTABA-JAMENEI.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66662f02-d557-11f1-8301-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-PORTADA-IRAN-MOJTABA-JAMENEI.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9dbd80d4-d653-11f1-8b8b-bd42c7a5c37a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 00:23:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66662f02-d557-11f1-8301-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-PORTADA-IRAN-MOJTABA-JAMENEI.jpg">© Vahid Salemi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Nine killed as business jet crashes into South Florida neighbourhood</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261101-nine-killed-as-business-jet-crashes-into-south-florida-neighbourhood</link><description>
A business jet plunged into a South Florida neighbourhood on Sunday, killing all nine people aboard and exploding into a fireball near homes and a busy road. The pilot had reported icing, precipitation and severe turbulence before the Learjet entered a steep dive, according to air traffic control recordings.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9e60d24-aa3e-11f1-8a9c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-06T210859Z-932383450-RC2WDNASZYYQ-RTRMADP-3-USA-CRASH-PLANE-MIAMI.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9e60d24-aa3e-11f1-8a9c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-06T210859Z-932383450-RC2WDNASZYYQ-RTRMADP-3-USA-CRASH-PLANE-MIAMI.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4623867a-d64e-11f1-8af9-cfcbd374c49b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 23:45:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9e60d24-aa3e-11f1-8a9c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-06T210859Z-932383450-RC2WDNASZYYQ-RTRMADP-3-USA-CRASH-PLANE-MIAMI.jpg">© Marco Bello, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French presidential candidate Édouard Philippe rejects centre-right primary</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261101-french-presidential-candidate-philippe-rejects-centre-right-primary</link><description>
French presidential candidate and former Prime Minister Édouard Philippe ruled out competing in a primary Sunday, following a proposal made last week by his rival Gabriel Attal to organize a vote to select a single centre-right candidate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8cd539c-d62e-11f1-9e78-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D63Z72Y.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8cd539c-d62e-11f1-9e78-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D63Z72Y.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">63eeae58-d63c-11f1-96cf-0771fbcaa233</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 21:51:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8cd539c-d62e-11f1-9e78-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D63Z72Y.jpg">© Julien de Rosa, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>UN’s peacekeeping mission in disputed Western Sahara ends after 35 years</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261101-un-s-peacekeeping-mission-in-disputed-western-sahara-ends-after-35-years</link><description>
The 35-year-old UN peacekeeping mission ⁠in the disputed Western ​Sahara region came to an end Sunday after the Security Council failed to ​renew its mandate. Morocco, which claims the region as its own, welcomed the decision, while its opponents from the Algeria-backed Polisario Front called it "unacceptable".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bfbe8ea-a712-11ec-a859-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/8013915005001.jpg.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bfbe8ea-a712-11ec-a859-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/8013915005001.jpg.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3766e2a6-d632-11f1-8508-ff00334a173f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 20:37:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bfbe8ea-a712-11ec-a859-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/8013915005001.jpg.png">© Mohamed Siali, EFE</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title><![CDATA[Michigan ‘Betrayal’ & Mid Term Manouvres]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261101-michigan-betrayal-mid-term-manouvres</link><description>
France 24’s Spotlight Presenter Gavin Lee assesses the last minute campaign dramas and takes an US election overview on the ‘must watch states’ alongside Professor Donald Green, Professor of Political Science at Columbia University and co-author of the definitive book ‘Get Out the Vote’, and foreign affairs analyst Laurie Dundon, who previously served in the U.S. State Department during the Clinton administration.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0fdb1aa-d62a-11f1-b8cd-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-PHOTO-US-POLITIQUE-0-00-01-00.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0fdb1aa-d62a-11f1-b8cd-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-PHOTO-US-POLITIQUE-0-00-01-00.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">babdc8ce-d62b-11f1-8248-bfd479b0b5c6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 19:37:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Route du Rhum yacht race sets off</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-route-du-rhum-yacht-race-sets-off</link><description>
The 115 sailors competing in the Route du Rhum set sail from Saint-Malo on Sunday in mild weather, embarking on a solo transatlantic crossing. The race began at 12:02 GMT, with boats heading along the Brittany coast in light winds towards a mandatory checkpoint near Cap Fréhel, where crowds had gathered to watch. One competitor, Nicolas d’Estais, described the conditions as ideal before boarding his yacht, Café Joyeux. Selina Sykes reports from Saint-Malo.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6c87276-d61a-11f1-a1b5-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-161049-161403-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6c87276-d61a-11f1-a1b5-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-161049-161403-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fc0227be-d61a-11f1-aeac-81a80d710011</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 17:46:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Thousands join Indian opposition protest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-join-indian-opposition-protest</link><description>
India’s opposition parties staged major protests in New Delhi on Sunday against Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s government and a nationwide voter list review that has fuelled demonstrations since the summer, led by the youth movement Cockroach Janta Party. Eliza Herbert reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cbb2c10-d61b-11f1-a32b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-170121-170312-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cbb2c10-d61b-11f1-a32b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-170121-170312-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">41b35b02-d61b-11f1-bc47-5d108f2cb387</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 17:45:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Oleshky: Evacuations during first humanitarian truce of war end</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/oleshky-evacuations-during-first-humanitarian-truce-of-war-end</link><description>
A successful evacuation. Residents of the city of Oleshky who had requested to be evacuated were reunited with their loved ones in Ukraine on Saturday, October 31. The city, located on the front line and under Russian occupation, is facing a humanitarian crisis, with civilians lacking even the most basic necessities. A localised ceasefire has been in place since Tuesday. France 24 correspondent Emmanuelle Chaze shares the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41a1e774-d606-11f1-9ff5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-150645-150857-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41a1e774-d606-11f1-9ff5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-150645-150857-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">46c17080-d606-11f1-99e7-67eb921d2022</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 17:44:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France reports largely peaceful protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-reports-largely-peaceful-protests</link><description>
France sees third consecutive weekend of protests over living costs and education, with more than 320,000 people taking to the streets. Most demonstrations remained peaceful, although police used tear gas to disperse clashes. Authorities reported more than 770 arrests nationwide. France24 journalist Jamie Smith-Maillet shares further insights.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c12466ee-d605-11f1-83e3-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-150107-150436-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c12466ee-d605-11f1-83e3-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-150107-150436-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c6131876-d605-11f1-8b4a-e7d7b19f4a2c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 15:50:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tech 24</category><title>Data centres on the ballot: could the AI infrastructure shape US midterms?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/data-centres-on-the-ballot-could-the-ai-infrastructure-shape-us-midterms</link><description>
Voters from Ohio to Illinois decide dozens of local measures on Tuesday, as opposition to the giant buildings powering AI cuts across party lines.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3162cc2-d604-11f1-8753-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/01-11-2026-13-59-ING33-PGM-B-FF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3162cc2-d604-11f1-8753-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/01-11-2026-13-59-ING33-PGM-B-FF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">445f6598-d5fe-11f1-ac91-57a86ac8fa86</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 15:11:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charlotte Lam</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Oleshky residents return to Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/oleshky-residents-return-to-ukraine</link><description>
Residents evacuated from Russian-occupied Oleshky have reached Ukrainian-held territory following a rare local truce. They described years of isolation, food shortages and regular shelling, with some saying they were forced to eat grass and dogs to survive. Seized by Russian forces in the early days of the 2022 invasion, the city remains cut off by the Dnipro River on one side and Russian troops on the other.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e35562ea-d5fb-11f1-b3a1-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-140341-140954-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e35562ea-d5fb-11f1-b3a1-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-140341-140954-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ebed22a8-d5fb-11f1-a03c-2d8e279fe3ae</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 14:56:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French high school blockades to restart on Monday, student unions say</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261101-french-high-school-blockades-to-restart-on-monday-student-unions-say</link><description>
The head of a student union said Sunday that high school blockades throughout France would restart on Monday. French President Emmanuel Macron has called for classes to resume after the government announced new measures to address the ongoing education crisis which student groups found insufficient.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a6963f2-d5ff-11f1-a635-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3KE3G7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a6963f2-d5ff-11f1-a635-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3KE3G7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84f0de28-d5fb-11f1-ba4f-01d389b6c400</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 14:31:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a6963f2-d5ff-11f1-a635-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3KE3G7.jpg">© Christophe Archambault, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Midterms: Democrats face leftward surge</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-democrats-face-leftward-surge</link><description>
As Democrats seek to regain control of Congress, divisions within the party are emerging over its future direction. A new wave of progressive candidates is pushing to shift priorities further to the left, challenging corporate money in politics and calling for universal healthcare, climate action and an end to police violence. Monte Francis reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0883ea4c-d5fb-11f1-958f-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-131203-131443-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0883ea4c-d5fb-11f1-958f-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-131203-131443-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0dbb5180-d5fb-11f1-9377-b5cd4537e7c7</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 13:56:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Poland rocked by Constitutional showdown</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/poland-rocked-by-constitutional-showdown</link><description>
Poland’s constitutional crisis deepened on Saturday as the European Commission urged President Karol Nawrocki to recognise new judges appointed by Prime Minister Donald Tusk. The standoff comes ahead of next year’s parliamentary election, with polls suggesting a close race between Tusk’s coalition and the nationalist right. Camille Corcoran reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a499c734-d5de-11f1-94fb-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-110736-110939-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a499c734-d5de-11f1-94fb-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-110736-110939-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a93435c2-d5de-11f1-bba3-75c6e95985cc</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 13:41:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Route du Rhum fleet ready to depart</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-route-du-rhum-fleet-ready-to-depart</link><description>
The Route du Rhum, billed as the world’s biggest solo transatlantic race, is set to depart from Saint-Malo in Brittany. Skippers will sail alone to Guadeloupe, with professionals and amateur sailors competing in the race, held every four years. Selina Sykes reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/870d1222-d5e1-11f1-8c01-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-111255-111454-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/870d1222-d5e1-11f1-8c01-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-111255-111454-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8ba5ed36-d5e1-11f1-8310-ffefaa430f3a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 13:12:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ceasefire in Ukraine's Kherson region ends after Russia refuses extension</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261101-localised-ceasefire-in-ukraine-s-kherson-region-set-to-end</link><description>
